Myril J Newton <myriln@aol.com> wrote:
> I just got a VAXstation 4000 model 90 : it has a scsi drive in it and I added
> an external CD drive.  both are recognized by the micros.

> I've tried booting from both no good.
> I dont have any HW docs.

> what is the syntax for booting either device.
> I have VMS on the CD and ????? on the disk.

Does the SCSI CD-ROM support 512-byte blocks, or just 2048-byte blocks?  You
need a drive that is set to support 512-byte blocks.

With the drive connected at the >>> prompt do the following:

>>> SHOW DEV

Then when you've identified the device name for the CD-ROM, do:

>>> BOOT DKA4

			Zane



