Uns Lider wrote:
 >  I also tried putting a terminator on the BNC jack.
> 


In standalone mode, DECHub gear need to see a properly terminated
thinwire segment, that means a T piece with 50 ohm terminator on
each end. In some instances, they need to see traffic and the terminal
servers like DECserver 90TL need to do a MOP boot to download drivers.

When plugged into a hub system, the thinwire segment is disabled.



