OK, it looks like I found the problem now, and it was pretty stupid.

The LEDs don't go out until the repeater sees a valid link on one of the
ports.

I was testing it with only a power supply attached, and assumed it was
broken because the LEDs were staying on. But then I plugged something into
one of the ports, and a few seconds later the LEDs went into the expected
state.

With it plugged into a DEChub-90, apparently the LEDs go out when it sees
a packet from one of the other modules.

I think I actually did have a power problem at first, when I was using the
long test leads. None of the LEDs would go out then. When I switched to
the direct connection, the self-test(?) LED would go out, but all the
others would stay on.

-- uns


