I just changed ISP and want to avoid getting spam. Hence the .nieuw in the
name part of the email address. I do not know what a RIP EFI is. A 5305 is
actually a Digital Server 5305, a white box Alpha that was sold to run NT
only. The 5305 is the equivalent of an AlphaServer 1200. The 5305, as the
AS1000 and AS1200, accepts memory only in pairs. One additional property: if
you install a 32 MB pair in slot 0 it will accept only one other pair of 32
MB dimms (in slot 1). If you want more memory in a 5305/1200 then a pair of
128 MB dimms in slot 0 is required.

