	What sort of keyboard are you plugging in?  A 101/102-key PC
style keyboard or an LK461 (DEC) style keyboard?  There is a environment
variable on the console, "kbd_hardware_type".  It can take one of two
values, "PCXAL" or "LK401" (or LK-something...I can't get to a console
at the moment).  I believe PCXAL is the default, but if you have an 
LK-style keyboard plugged in, you'd do better to change to the "other" 
value.  Similarly, if kbd_hardware_type is set to the LK-value but
you've plugged in a PC keyboard, it may work better if you switch 
back to PCXAL.

	HTH, Ken
