> M7555-RQDX3 from a MicroVAX II 

Except for the old paper tape software, you are going to be pretty
much limited to RT-11.   This system only supports 16-bit addressing,
so you can only put 60KB *maximum*[0] in it.

DO *NOT* install any cards which support 22-bit addressing into that
backplane!!!   The high-order address bit pins are used by the LSI-11
CPU for special purposes.   This eliminates all modern disk controllers.

[0] Normally, 16-bit PDP-11 systems had a 4KW (8KB) I/O page, for a
     maximum usable memory of 28KW (56KB).   However, the LSI-11 can
     have a 2KW (4KB) I/O page.

Alan



