>And does it go in the left or right pair of slots. 

I think you have most of a 16kword 11/03.  ISTR the General Robotics
card was similar to a MXV11, but with 18bits worth of ram. It doesn't
belong to that 11/03, and there is something weird about those GR
cards.

>
>Also, I'd like to add a disc controller and operating system. Is 
>it best to use a modern SCSI-type Q-bus card. or can I fit a 
>M7555-RQDX3 from a MicroVAX II 

No chance!  A RX01 is as good as you will get.

>Is this all going to go into the four slot backplane, As one of
>the slots will need to contain a card with boot-loader proms, As
>this CPU doesn't have them on-board.
>

The good news is, that if  you're using a PC as a terminal, you don't
need a hardware boot. Jumper the cpu to halt on power up, load and
start the bootstrap from the PC using emulated console ODT commands.
You can use RT11, slowly, with TU58 emulation on the PC, given a
second serial interface, but realistically, IIRC, I'm not sure that
you have a useable console interface.  I'd suggest that your first
task is to power up the 11 with the halt switch down, and establish
communications with console ODT.

Old 11/03s are not totally useless: I used one through the 80s with a
64bit i/o card as a burglar alarm system, and the young kids have it
now to control their model railway.  

To get chapter and verse on what you have, walk over to alt.sys.pdp11.

Regards,

David P.
 


