I think you have two separate companies mixed up.  Memory isn't always
reliable but an S-100 based machine made by DCC in the early 80's sounds
familiar.  There were quite a few S-100 vendors building everything from Z80
to x86 to 68K on the same backplane.  No relation to DEC though I'm sure the
name was an attempt to borrow a little glory.

Try comp.os.cpm and see if anyone recognizes it.  If you can post pictures
somewhere that really helps in identifying "screwdriver systems" assembled
from other vendors' boards.  Are there any names or model numbers on the
boards in the backplane, and how many slots does it have?
