Think VMS as a super-set of UN*X.

Check out http://www.compaq.openvms.com/doc/ and browse the
documentation for a taste of it.

There is also at least one VMS machine (Google for "Hobbes the VAX")
where you can get a Telnet account.

> And what about the hardware? Is it worth even trying to locate more
> cpu's, ram, hard drives?

Runs on most Alpha's (some "white box" Alpha's are too brain dead run
anything but Micro$hit, but some can be reflashed with SRM) and all
VAXes. Can be made to run Alpha Multias (OpenVMS V7.2).

SCSI disk and ethernet card compatibility was a problem on early
versions. Specifications are less stringent now, but still not as
"loosey-goosey" as WhineBloze.

Most small Alphas take 72-pin FPM SIMMs (n x 36).

