>anyone ever tried to do this?  If so, what (if anything) must be done
>to configure the mouse?  The system currently has Tru64 Unix installed
>(I'm not sure which version), although I might switch to NetBSD.

I think you're out of luck expecting any PC mouse to work - they are not
electrically compatible.  $45 eh ?  I'd expect to see a whole Vaxstation
sold for less, including mouse !  You could also try looking for the
original "hockey puck" mouse, which I am fairly sure is 100% compatible -
it's a VSXXX-AA, or possibly -BA.

>Of course, if anyone has a working VSXXX-GA mouse they'd be willing to
>sell for a good price, I'd consider that too.

Have you tried giving it a good clean ?  Pop the ball out and you may well
see an accumulation of fluff on the rollers inside, or the ball may be
dirty.  Also, these mice are rather fussy about mats - they don't work at
all well on shiny mats.  A genuine Digital neoprene mat is the business.


	John


