Hello folks,

Well, I read some Alpha ARM manual and some technical manuals (found on
Digitial Documentation Library) about AlphaPC series.  I learned that system
(SROM) had loaded Flash ROM image into main memory from 87.FFF8.0000 and
started executation at the beginning of ROM image at location 0 or
destination address in ROM header when system power was turned on.

Also, I learned that Alpha instructions are RISC-type (much simple
instructions) like PDP-10 instructions.  They are 32-bit wide opcodes.
Also, they does not use status register (condition codes).  For example, BIS
R31,R31,R31 instruction are NOP because R31 acts like /dev/zero or
OpenVMS NL:, etc...

I read some comp.os.vms faqs (ALPHA8 and ALPHA13) about Alpha OpenVMS and
AlphaPC 164 series.  I learned that they can be booted with only SCSI
controllers.  Does Alpha OpenVMS support AlphaPC 164 series with SCSI
controllers?

According to AlphaPC technical manuals, I now am looking for Alpha
Motherboards SDK kit.  On Digital/Compaq/HP site, I was looking for that but
only found SDK manuals.  Does anyone know where is that to get or order?

Thank you,
Tim Stark




