I did an experiment here this weekend and now need some help
straightening out the results.  <sigh>

I was investigating support options for an HSZ50.  Since we had a spare
HSZ40 (actually, a SWXCR-05), I suggested that it could be used as a
backup.

We tested that this weekend.  The HSZ40 was working properly.  Shutdown
and remove the HSZ50 and its cache.  Install the HSZ40 in its place. 
Power backup up.

The HSZ40 booted fine, but had the configuration for its old box.  So, I
started with a "SET THIS_CONTROLLER INITIAL_CONFIGURATION".

After the HSZ40 rebooted, its licenses were all INVALID!

One odd think I noticed was that when setting the initial configuration,
the HSZ40 reported that it was loading the configuration from a drive
that had SAVE_CONFIGURATION set, but it didn't actually load the new
configutation.  Could trying to load a HSZ50 configuration hose a HSZ40?

Also, I didn't notice before this, but "SHOW THIS" reports that the
controller is a SWXCR-04 when it is really a SWXCR-05.  (What is the
difference between a -04 and -05 anyways?)

The serial number on the controller is still set correctly.  The
controller seems to work correctly, it just doesn't have any valid
licenses anymore.

The HSZ40 is running V31Z-4.

So my questions are:

What causes this?

How can the licenses be restored?

Were there any controllers sold that didn't have these licenses enabled?

Thanx!


